{"title":"2021 Fall AMC 12B Problems/Problem 8","text":"<div class=\"mw-content-ltr mw-parser-output\" lang=\"en\" dir=\"ltr\"><div id=\"toc\" class=\"toc\" role=\"navigation\" aria-labelledby=\"mw-toc-heading\"><input type=\"checkbox\" role=\"button\" id=\"toctogglecheckbox\" class=\"toctogglecheckbox\" style=\"display:none\" /><div class=\"toctitle\" lang=\"en\" dir=\"ltr\"><h2 id=\"mw-toc-heading\">Contents</h2><span class=\"toctogglespan\"><label class=\"toctogglelabel\" for=\"toctogglecheckbox\"></label></span></div>\n<ul>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-1\"><a href=\"#Problem\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">1</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Problem</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-2\"><a href=\"#Solution_1_(Area)\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">2</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Solution 1 (Area)</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-3\"><a href=\"#Solution_2\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">3</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Solution 2</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-4\"><a href=\"#Video_Solution_(Under_2_min!)\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">4</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Video Solution (Under 2 min!)</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-5\"><a href=\"#Video_Solution_by_TheBeautyofMath\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">5</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Video Solution by TheBeautyofMath</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-6\"><a href=\"#See_Also\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">6</span> <span class=\"toctext\">See Also</span></a></li>\n</ul>\n</div>\n\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Problem\">Problem</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2021_Fall_AMC_12B_Problems/Problem_8&amp;action=edit&amp;section=1\" title=\"Edit section: Problem\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>The product of the lengths of the two congruent sides of an obtuse isosceles triangle is equal to the product of the base and twice the triangle's height to the base. What is the measure, in degrees, of the vertex angle of this triangle?\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/0/e/00e7b6dc4bc63e2920a6efe04d8de993028b3611.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\textbf{(A)} \\: 105 \\qquad\\textbf{(B)} \\: 120 \\qquad\\textbf{(C)} \\: 135 \\qquad\\textbf{(D)} \\: 150 \\qquad\\textbf{(E)} \\: 165$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"434\" height=\"18\" />\n</p>\n<h2><span id=\"Solution_1_.28Area.29\"></span><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Solution_1_(Area)\">Solution 1 (Area)</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2021_Fall_AMC_12B_Problems/Problem_8&amp;action=edit&amp;section=2\" title=\"Edit section: Solution 1 (Area)\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>Let the lengths of the two congruent sides of the triangle be <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/6/e/26eeb5258ca5099acf8fe96b2a1049c48c89a5e6.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$x$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"12\" height=\"10\" />, then the product desired is <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/6/b/76b2878564ab19b80abb21ba964abe90fe120846.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$x^2$\" width=\"16\" height=\"15\" />.\n</p><p>Notice that the product of the base and twice the height is <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/7/c/c7cab1a05e1e0c1d51a6a219d96577a16b7abf9d.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$4$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" /> times the area of the triangle.\n</p><p>Set the vertex angle to be <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/7/d/c7d457e388298246adb06c587bccd419ea67f7e8.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$a$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"10\" />, we derive the equation:\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/2/d/72db6f0e9cc49508085daa9fb52c141b78893cde.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$x^2=4\\left(\\frac{1}{2}x^2\\sin(a)\\right)$\" style=\"vertical-align: -18px\" width=\"162\" height=\"45\" />\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/7/a/b7a848ed43085b80e26a91646f836632a94bb307.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\sin(a)=\\frac{1}{2}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -13px\" width=\"85\" height=\"38\" />\n</p><p>As the triangle is obtuse, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/9/8/2/982babfafb9882edd7fb8717f4d8694255f04d00.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$a=150^\\circ$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"71\" height=\"15\" /> only. We get <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/b/c/3bc25055627cdcc90f2d7eb67e5f705f7ad31939.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\boxed{\\textbf{(D)} \\ 150}.$\" style=\"vertical-align: -11px\" width=\"80\" height=\"30\" />\n</p><p>~Wilhelm Z\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Solution_2\">Solution 2</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2021_Fall_AMC_12B_Problems/Problem_8&amp;action=edit&amp;section=3\" title=\"Edit section: Solution 2\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>Denote by <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/7/d/c7d457e388298246adb06c587bccd419ea67f7e8.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$a$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"10\" /> the length of each congruent side. Denote by <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/2/e/52e8ed7a3ba22130ad3984eb2cd413406475a689.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\theta$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" /> the degree measure of each acute angle.\nDenote by <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/c/1/2c175f60eecef1de7560c3bdea495d69f26f719d.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\phi$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"13\" height=\"18\" /> the degree measure of the obtuse angle.\n</p><p>Hence, this problem tells us the following relationship:\n<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/3/2/c328ec8657d0713415c84b2d34b0e134f138e24e.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[ a^2 = 2 a \\cos \\theta \\cdot 2 a \\sin \\theta . \\]\" width=\"172\" height=\"15\" />\n</p><p>Hence,\n<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/1/3/f1330bba1be5f954878773986d05350e83dcdbbf.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\begin{align*} 1 &amp; = 2 \\cdot 2 \\sin \\theta \\cos \\theta \\\\ &amp; = 2 \\sin 2 \\theta \\\\ &amp; = 2 \\sin \\left( 180^\\circ - 2 \\theta \\right) \\\\ &amp; = 2 \\sin \\phi . \\end{align*}\" width=\"157\" height=\"91\" />\n</p><p>Hence, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/a/3/3/a3307c329690d9053e87bfd762ea8dea76388d01.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\phi = 150^\\circ$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"72\" height=\"18\" />.\n</p><p>Therefore, the answer is <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/a/6/6a652f00eb29869385d55f49c026d6fc11974194.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\boxed{\\textbf{(D) }150}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -11px\" width=\"76\" height=\"30\" />.\n</p><p>~Steven Chen (www.professorchenedu.com)\n</p><p><br />\n</p>\n<h2><span id=\"Video_Solution_.28Under_2_min.21.29\"></span><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Video_Solution_(Under_2_min!)\">Video Solution (Under 2 min!)</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2021_Fall_AMC_12B_Problems/Problem_8&amp;action=edit&amp;section=4\" title=\"Edit section: Video Solution (Under 2 min!)\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p><a rel=\"nofollow\" class=\"external free\" href=\"https://youtu.be/nXnS6pn8iJc\">https://youtu.be/nXnS6pn8iJc</a>\n</p><p><i>~Education, the Study of Everything</i>\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Video_Solution_by_TheBeautyofMath\">Video Solution by TheBeautyofMath</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2021_Fall_AMC_12B_Problems/Problem_8&amp;action=edit&amp;section=5\" title=\"Edit section: Video Solution by TheBeautyofMath\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p><a rel=\"nofollow\" class=\"external free\" href=\"https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=4qgYrCYG-qw&amp;t=795\">https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=4qgYrCYG-qw&amp;t=795</a>\n</p><p>~IceMatrix\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"See_Also\">See Also</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2021_Fall_AMC_12B_Problems/Problem_8&amp;action=edit&amp;section=6\" title=\"Edit section: See Also\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<table class=\"wikitable\" style=\"margin:0.5em auto; font-size:95%; border:1px solid black; width:80%;\">\n<tbody><tr>\n<td style=\"background:#ccf;text-align:center;\" colspan=\"2\"><b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2021_Fall_AMC_12B\" title=\"2021 Fall AMC 12B\">2021 Fall AMC 12B</a></b> (<b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2021_Fall_AMC_12B_Problems\" title=\"2021 Fall AMC 12B Problems\">Problems</a></b> • <b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2021_Fall_AMC_12B_Answer_Key\" title=\"2021 Fall AMC 12B Answer Key\">Answer Key</a></b> • <a rel=\"nofollow\" class=\"external text\" href=\"http://www.artofproblemsolving.com/community/c13\">Resources</a>)\n</td></tr>\n<tr>\n<td width=\"50%\" align=\"center\" rowspan=\"1\">Preceded&#160;by<br /><b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2021_Fall_AMC_12B_Problems/Problem_7\" title=\"2021 Fall AMC 12B Problems/Problem 7\">Problem 7</a></b>\n</td>\n<td width=\"50%\" align=\"center\" rowspan=\"1\">Followed&#160;by<br /><b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2021_Fall_AMC_12B_Problems/Problem_9\" title=\"2021 Fall AMC 12B Problems/Problem 9\">Problem 9</a></b>\n</td></tr>\n<tr>\n<td colspan=\"2\" style=\"text-align:center;\"><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2021_Fall_AMC_12B_Problems/Problem_1\" title=\"2021 Fall AMC 12B Problems/Problem 1\">1</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2021_Fall_AMC_12B_Problems/Problem_2\" title=\"20